<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Resources that are referenced only by name at runtime.

  PokéPod hands these two drawables to flutter_local_notifications as *strings*
  from Dart (lib/features/notifications/notification_service.dart):

      AndroidInitializationSettings('@drawable/notification_icon')   // channel default
      icon: '@drawable/notification_flame'                           // per-notification

  AAPT2's resource shrinker only inspects references it can see — manifest,
  layout XML and compiled code — so it stripped both from release builds. On a
  release device the plugin then failed at startup with

      PlatformException(invalid_icon, The resource @drawable/notification_icon
      could not be found.)

  and streak reminders never ran (debug builds are not shrunk, so this was
  release-only). Keeping the two drawables by name restores them without
  turning resource shrinking off for anything else.

  The widget drawables deliberately need no entry here: widget_card_bg,
  widget_chip_bg and widget_pokeball are referenced from layout XML, and
  launch_background from styles.xml, so the shrinker already keeps those.

  The same shrinker also removes res/raw/notification.mp3, which is named only
  from Dart (RawResourceAndroidNotificationSound('notification') on the channel
  and on every reminder). AAPT2 cannot see either reference, so getIdentifier()
  returns 0 and flutter_local_notifications rejects the schedule outright with

      PlatformException(invalid_sound, The resource notification could not be
      found. Please make sure it has been added as a raw resource ...)

  before any alarm is set - so in a release build no streak reminder was ever
  armed at all, even though initialize() and the channel both succeeded. Keeping
  the sound by name is the whole fix.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@drawable/notification_icon,@drawable/notification_flame,@raw/notification" />
